					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE: RESET PHASE\n\nIn the example we’ve got a Sine oscillator moving the rectangles up and down.\nThe red rectangle is the original signal, the blue rectangle is the signal being followed.\n\nAs you can see, the blue signal is slightly delayed.\nThis is even more clear when you hit the reset phase button.\nThe original signal will immediately jump to 0, while the blue rectangle will “catch up” instead due to the Envelope Follower."
					}
				},
